         "notes": "Shared Mail Server: create an AlwaysData mailbox and authenticate on smtp-<username>.alwaysdata.net (SMTP AUTH, e.g. a Python smtplib or PHPMailer script), then send a message with a forged From on the hosted domain. MAIL FROM aligns with the hosted domain (in SPF), so DMARC passes on the SPF branch even under p=reject. Signed d=alwaysdata.net s=default (valid, not aligned)."},
