         "dkim": "alwaysdata.net:s=default",
         "notes": "Local MTA of the shared host (e.g. a PHP mail()/PHPMailer script, `mail -f` / Sender field): submits through the host with NO SMTP authentication (auth bypass). MAIL FROM is aligned with the hosted domain (in SPF), so DMARC is bypassed even under p=reject. The message is DKIM-signed by alwaysdata.net (s=default), NOT aligned with the forged From, but DMARC still passes via SPF alignment (the SPF-OR-DKIM rule), and the valid signature avoids an R_DKIM_NA penalty.", "transport": "local_submission"}
